Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.45,0:00:05.84,Default,,0,0,0,,To keep our evaluation scientifically honest,\Nwe also have to highlight three clear limitations.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:06.51,0:00:10.24,Default,,0,0,0,,First, achieving zero false\Nresolutions across both model
Dialogue: 0,0:00:10.24,0:00:14.35,Default,,0,0,0,,families owes a great deal to the\Ntight coupling between FinalizeGate's
Dialogue: 0,0:00:14.52,0:00:18.45,Default,,0,0,0,,seven hardcoded mechanism rules and\Nour synthetic benchmark scenarios.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:18.81,0:00:22.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Testing on out-of-distribution,\Nunstructured production logs is
Dialogue: 0,0:00:22.22,0:00:26.21,Default,,0,0,0,,essential to measure true hallucination\Nresistance when hard rules weaken.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:26.51,0:00:30.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Second, our automatic scorer currently checks\Nculprit service and failure mode match,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:31.07,0:00:34.52,Default,,0,0,0,,even though the oracle already defines\Nacceptable evidence support sets —
Dialogue: 0,0:00:34.53,0:00:38.52,Default,,0,0,0,,incorporating support-set coverage and\Nre-centering paired bootstrap statistics
Dialogue: 0,0:00:38.52,0:00:42.34,Default,,0,0,0,,onto Dynamic are immediate,\Nhigh-leverage upgrades. Third,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:42.93,0:00:48.15,Default,,0,0,0,,our cross-model finding on incident_4035\Npoints directly to an on-demand Verifier:
Dialogue: 0,0:00:48.60,0:00:52.56,Default,,0,0,0,,keep Dynamic as the fast, economical\Ndefault, and trigger an independent
Dialogue: 0,0:00:52.56,0:00:56.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Verifier only when competing-mechanism\Nor counterfactual signals appear.
